What was taken from upstream
----------------------------
Only the *observable wire format* and facts that are required for compatibility:

  * the default level table (trace 10 … fatal 60), read from lib/constants.js;
  * the shape of a log line, produced by lib/proto.js `_asJson`
    (`level`, `time`, `pid`, `hostname`, bindings, message key, trailing \n);
  * pino's value coerced semantics: non-finite numbers become `null`,
    `undefined`/function values are dropped, circular structures become
    `[Circular]` via safe-stable-stringify;
  * the default redaction censor string `[Redacted]`;
  * the interaction between `nestedKey` and redaction paths, verified by
    running the repository build rather than reading documentation.

No source file from pino is included in this directory. The example service
imports the repository's own `pino.js` at runtime rather than copying it.

Third-party runtime dependencies
-------------------------------
None. The report embeds only hand-written JavaScript and CSS. `puppeteer-core`
is a development dependency used by the browser test suite and is not part of
the generated report.

Sample data
-----------
`examples/traffic-service/out/traffic.ndjson` was produced by running the
pino build in this repository behind a local HTTP server on 2026-10-22.
It contains no personal data: the hostname is a fixed `base` binding
(`lab-node-01`), the only authorisation value sent by the driver is the literal
string `demo-token-not-a-secret`, and pino redacts it before it reaches disk.
The accompanying `traffic.manifest.json` records the command, versions, counts
and SHA-256 of the file.
